# Raw inputs are third-party data under their own licences. Some forbid
# redistribution (Sci Rep 2025 supplementary data is CC BY-NC-ND 4.0, whose
# NoDerivatives clause covers sharing parts of it), so nothing under data/raw/
# is committed. Each subdirectory carries a manifest.json recording where its
# files came from, under what licence, and their checksums; those manifests are
# the reproducible part and are tracked.
# `data/raw/*` alone would not do: re-including a subdirectory re-includes
# everything in it, since the exclusion only matched the directory's parent.
data/raw/**
!data/raw/**/
!data/raw/**/manifest.json
!data/raw/**/SHA256SUMS
# The record of which sources were searched: no third-party data, so it is
# tracked. A source that is "not public" is not the same as one that does not
# exist, and that distinction is only useful if it survives in the repository.
!data/raw/_searched.json

# Generated; safe to delete at any time.
data/work/

# Build output and test caches.
# The trailing glob matters: there are three build directories, not one.
# `engine/target/` alone left target-fp/ and target-lin/ tracked, which put
# 633 of the 669 files in the first commit's index.
engine/target*/
.hypothesis/
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# Experiment outputs live under data/work/, which is already ignored. The
# predictions of py/inclusion.py are the exception worth keeping: they are the
# record that the rule was stated before the transfers were run, so a copy is
# tracked as docs/inclusion_predictions.json.
